{
  "title": "A Navy SEAL and His K9 Asked for Ten Days' Shelter—Two Sisters Never Guessed He'd Save Their Ranch",
  "description": "He asked for ten days and a warm place for his dog. He ended up holding the one thing that could save their ranch.<br><br>Cole Brandt spent twelve years as a Navy SEAL. Now his truck is dead on a Montana highway, and all he has left is Gunner, a retired military working dog. At the Sutter ranch gate he asks Maggie for ten days of work in exchange for a roof and a hot meal. She says no. Then a dozen cattle break through a leaning fence and bolt for the icy creek, and Cole has them turned around before anyone even knows his name.<br><br>Maggie and her sister Wren lost their father in October. They&apos;re four payments behind, the bank wants a new plan by the twentieth, and a polite land buyer named Dennis Kroll keeps raising his offer and driving slowly past their fence. Cole fixes the roof, the water line and the porch their dad never got to paint. Then one night Gunner growls at the cabin door, and down on Willow Creek Cole finds something nobody was meant to see. But before he can tell Maggie, she tells him he has somewhere else to be.<br><br>👉 Watch till the end — find out what Gunner found on that creek, and what Maggie does when it&apos;s finally her call.<br><br>If you love stories about loyal dogs and second chances, subscribe for a new story every week.<br><br>This is a fictional story made for entertainment. All characters, places and events are invented.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/navyseal\">#NavySEAL</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/k9\">#K9</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/story\">#Story</a>",
